{"Title":"An Act providing for a universal basic income for youth aging out of foster care","BillNumber":"S114","DocketNumber":"SD2292","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"L M0","Name":"Liz Miranda","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L M0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T15:11:58.457"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"L M0","Name":"Liz Miranda","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L M0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T15:11:58.4566667"},{"Id":"V_H1","Name":"Vanna Howard","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/V_H1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T13:42:41.66"},{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-07T13:07:50.5133333"},{"Id":"S_G1","Name":"Sean Garballey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_G1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T12:36:53.6666667"},{"Id":"SND0","Name":"Sal N. DiDomenico","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SND0","ResponseDate":"2023-05-22T11:59:14.0833333"},{"Id":"RLR0","Name":"Rebecca L. Rausch","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RLR0","ResponseDate":"2023-07-11T11:55:15.3933333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S114/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Miranda, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 114) of Liz Miranda, Jason M. Lewis, Vanna Howard and Sean Garballey for legislation to provide for a universal basic income for youth aging out of foster care.  Children, Families and Persons with Disabilities.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 119 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after section 23B the following section:-\r\n\tSection 23C. The department shall, subject to appropriation, provide a cash stipend of $1,000 per month for 5 years to any individual formerly under the custody, care or responsibility of the department, but have transitioned from the custody, care or responsibility of the department upon reaching the age of 23.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J13","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J13"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}